# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
# The eol attribute overrides core.autocrlf, so Git no longer promises to
# rewrite the working copy to CRLF on Windows and stops warning about it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The application page is hash-locked: desktop/web/embed_test.go records the
# exact SHA-256 and size of the shipped copy. Any end-of-line conversion during
# a checkout would silently break that lock, so the page and its source of
# truth are marked as binary text (-text) and must survive byte for byte.
# These rules come last so they win over the "* text=auto eol=lf" rule above.
/src/app/index.html -text
/desktop/web/index.html -text
